From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:30:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp-display: Take the GPU vote on the
 J604 as well

The retained PMP vote bridge serves the DISP vote on the J713 and the
J604, but its AGX (GPU) entry points refuse every board but the J713.
The J604 PMP publishes the same soc-device table as the J713, and the
bridge already validates the AGX entry of that table when it registers
(agx_table_valid) and refuses a GPU vote if it is not there.

Serve the GPU entry points on every apple_pmp_display_board(), as the
display ones are. The consumer checks stay: the voter must be the
"apple,agx-t8132" node that the "gpu" alias names and whose apple,pmp
phandle is the bridge's PMP. The entry points keep their j713 names to
keep this change small.

Nothing calls these on the J604 until the G16 driver admits it.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit c958d6b767010d1ba41e91f172020b0ab7dddc2e)
(cherry picked from commit 5030f48979b41565a4313cd489a140cf5e9a7e43)
(cherry picked from commit 660583d6e7276693de3d6da4ba47487a31b2b5a2)
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c       |  7 +++----
 include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h | 16 ++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
index 632982ddc3..46c498e9f7 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
@@ -322,7 +322,6 @@ static struct apple_pmp_display *pmp_power_consumer(struct device *consumer,
 	if (apple_pmp_display_board()) {
 		/* Both consumers must name the exact boot-profile node. */
 		if ((kind != PMP_POWER_AGX && kind != PMP_POWER_DISP) || !consumer->of_node ||
-		    (kind == PMP_POWER_AGX && !apple_pmp_j713_board()) ||
 		    !of_device_is_compatible(consumer->of_node,
 			kind == PMP_POWER_AGX ? "apple,agx-t8132" : "apple,t8132-dcp"))
 			return ERR_PTR(-ENODEV);
@@ -521,7 +520,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_display_prepare);
 
 int apple_pmp_j713_gpu_prepare(struct device *consumer)
 {
-	return apple_pmp_j713_board() ? pmp_power_prepare(consumer, PMP_POWER_AGX) : -ENODEV;
+	return apple_pmp_display_board() ? pmp_power_prepare(consumer, PMP_POWER_AGX) : -ENODEV;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_gpu_prepare);
 
@@ -539,7 +538,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_display_check_release);
 
 int apple_pmp_j713_gpu_check(struct device *consumer)
 {
-	return apple_pmp_j713_board() ? pmp_power_check(consumer, PMP_POWER_AGX, false) : -ENODEV;
+	return apple_pmp_display_board() ? pmp_power_check(consumer, PMP_POWER_AGX, false) : -ENODEV;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_gpu_check);
 
@@ -557,6 +556,6 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_display_put);
 
 int apple_pmp_j713_gpu_get(struct device *consumer)
 {
-	return apple_pmp_j713_board() ? pmp_power_get(consumer, PMP_POWER_AGX) : -ENODEV;
+	return apple_pmp_display_board() ? pmp_power_get(consumer, PMP_POWER_AGX) : -ENODEV;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_gpu_get);
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h
index e3f8122ff3..ce60120085 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h
@@ -13,9 +13,9 @@ static inline bool apple_pmp_j713_board(void)
 }
 
 /*
- * Boards whose retained PMP session carries the DISP vote. The J604 PMP
- * publishes the same soc-device table as the J713; its AGX vote is not
- * qualified, so the GPU entry points below stay J713-only.
+ * Boards whose retained PMP session carries the DISP and AGX votes. The
+ * J604 PMP publishes the same soc-device table as the J713, and the bridge
+ * checks the AGX entry of that table before it accepts a GPU vote.
  */
 static inline bool apple_pmp_display_board(void)
 {
@@ -44,11 +44,11 @@ struct apple_pmp_display *apple_pmp_display_bound_owner(struct device *dev);
 
 /* Retained votes share the existing PMP owner's untagged request stream.
  * Prepare is probe-only; supplier links persist until reboot, and so do
- * accepted votes, except that the DCP releases its DISP vote while it has
- * powered the display domains down (put) and takes it again (get). Before
- * that it asks, changing nothing, whether the vote can be released now and
- * taken again later (check_release). The display entry points serve every
- * apple_pmp_display_board(), the GPU ones only the J713.
+ * accepted DISP/AGX votes, except that the DCP releases its DISP vote while
+ * it has powered the display domains down (put) and takes it again (get).
+ * Before that it asks, changing nothing, whether the vote can be released
+ * now and taken again later (check_release). The display and GPU entry
+ * points serve every apple_pmp_display_board().
  */
 int apple_pmp_j713_display_prepare(struct device *consumer);
 int apple_pmp_j713_display_get(struct device *consumer);
-- 
